        "PMC12463061::web::018::effect_of_strain_rate_on_yield_strength"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Baseline TiVNbTa has a room-temperature yield strength of approximately 800 MPa.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Baseline TiVNbTa has a yield strength of approximately 330 MPa at 1273 K.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Baseline TiVNbTa has a compressive strength of approximately 423 MPa at 1273 K.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed intervention is to add approximately 2–5 at.% Mo to TiVNbTa and apply a precipitation-promoting heat treatment.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Adding 2–5 at.% Mo and heat treating the alloy will form fine Mo-rich precipitates in the BCC matrix.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Mo-rich precipitates will be uniformly dispersed at nano-to-submicron length scales.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Dispersed precipitates can impede dislocation motion and produce precipitation strengthening in a continuous BCC matrix.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5995863::web::017::discussion"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mo-rich precipitates will impede grain-boundary sliding in modified TiVNbTa.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Maintaining a continuous BCC matrix containing discrete precipitates can preserve ductility while providing strengthening.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5995863::web::017::discussion"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Mo modification will increase TiVNbTa yield strength at 1273 K by at least 25% relative to the 330 MPa baseline.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Mo modification will improve high-temperature creep resistance.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Mo modification will have minimal adverse impact on room-temperature ductility.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5995863::web::017::discussion"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Mo modification will preserve thermal conductivity sufficient for heat transfer between W and CuCrZr.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Restricting Mo to no more than approximately 5 at.% will avoid coarse or brittle phases that would compromise ductility or thermal conduction.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed operating and test range is 300–1273 K under static and cyclic loading.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Severe lattice distortion in BCC NbTaTiV can obstruct edge-dislocation glide and contribute to resistance to plastic deformation.",
      "field": "supporting_evidence_ids",
      "needs_support": true,
